60/pdf", "content-type": "unspecified", "content-version": "vor", "intended-application": "similarity-checking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2021, 4, 19]], "date-time": "2021-04-19T16:17:37Z", "timestamp": 1618849057000}, "score": 21.15311, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.degruyter.com/document/doi/10.1355/9789814379960/html"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[1991, 1, 1]]}, "ISBN": ["9789814379960"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1355/9789814379960", "published": {"date-parts": [[1991, 1, 1]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 24]], "date-time": "2026-03-24T11:10:38Z", "timestamp": 1774350638370, "version": "3.50.1"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>Multi-agentic AI systems (MAS) amplify capability by distributing work across specialized, semi-autonomous agents, but they also expand the attack surface with greater tools, more boundaries, more inter-agent communications, and more chances for emergent behaviors to go wrong. As we highlight in this document, security by design for MAS will require intertwining governance and compliance aligned to AI risk frameworks (NIST AI RMF) and evolving standards and regulations (ISO/IEC 42001, EU AI Act), secure architectures with strong isolation (sandboxing) and least privilege enforcements, MAS-specific threat modeling, pre-deployment and continuous security testing that includes red teaming of inter-Agent channels, and runtime monitoring and response. Moreover, security must be embedded at every stage of Agent development, governance, and execution.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.6334398", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 24]], "date-time": "2026-03-24T09:05:44Z", "timestamp": 1774343144000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Security-by-Design for Multi-Agentic AI Systems"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6275-2724", "authenticated-orcid": true, "given": "Shaurya", "family": "Jauhari", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "78", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 3, 24]], "date-time": "2026-03-24T09:05:44Z", "timestamp": 1774343144000}, "score": 20.726522, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=6334398"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6334398", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 3]], "date-time": "2024-05-03T18:04:21Z", "timestamp": 1714759461120}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9780127616506", "type": "print"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[1969]]}, "DOI": "10.1016/b978-0-12-761650-6.50014-2", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2013, 11, 19]], "date-time": "2013-11-19T12:53:48Z", "timestamp": 1384865628000}, "page": "221", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Conversion Table for Rf and Rm"], "prefix": "10.1016", "member": "78", "container-title": ["Separation Methods in Organic Chemistry and Biochemistry"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2018, 10, 9]], "date-time": "2018-10-09T17:23:27Z", "timestamp": 1539105807000}, "score": 20.52232, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/B9780127616506500142"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[1969]]}, "ISBN": ["9780127616506"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-12-761650-6.50014-2", "published": {"date-parts": [[1969]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 14]], "date-time": "2026-08-14T15:29:11Z", "timestamp": 1786721351584, "version": "build-2736575974"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "group-title": "SSRN", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "abstract": "<jats:p>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span&gt;This whitepaper introduces the AFuller F7-LAS\u2122 &amp;nbsp;(Fuller 7-Layer Agentic AI Security) model, a practical&amp;nbsp; for analyzing and securing agentic AI systems in enterprise environments. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The model focuses on seven layers, from system prompts, RAG, and the planner through tools and policy engines, down to sandboxed execution and monitoring. The goal is to provide security architects and practitioners with a clear, layered&amp;nbsp; to reason about risk and design controls for AI systems that can take actions, not just generate text.&lt;/p&gt;</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.5848743", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 9]], "date-time": "2026-01-09T12:18:42Z", "timestamp": 1767961122000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Securing Agentic AI: The AFuller F7-LAS\u2122 (7-Layer) Model: Fuller 7-Layer Agentic AI Security (F7-LAS\u2122 )"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"given": "Anthony L.", "family": "Fuller", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "78", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 8, 14]], "date-time": "2026-08-14T14:35:28Z", "timestamp": 1786718128000}, "score": 20.497915, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=5848743"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.5848743", "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "subtype": "preprint"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 3]], "date-time": "2024-05-03T18:41:27Z", "timestamp": 1714761687312}, "reference-count": 21, "publisher": "Elsevier", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9780433305033", "type": "print"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": 