78-0-433-30503-3.50031-6_bib19", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "first-page": "851", "DOI": "10.1021/ac60125a035", "volume": "29", "author": "Sundt", "year": "1957", "journal-title": "Anal. Chem."}, {"key": "10.1016/B978-0-433-30503-3.50031-6_bib20", "unstructured": "Trafford, D. J. H., and Edwards, R. W. H., unpublished observations."}, {"key": "10.1016/B978-0-433-30503-3.50031-6_bib21", "doi-asserted-by": "crossref", "first-page": "6", "DOI": "10.1126/science.111.2871.6", "volume": "111", "author": "Zaffaroni", "year": "1950", "journal-title": "Science"}], "container-title": ["Chromatography"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2022, 3, 13]], "date-time": "2022-03-13T03:55:49Z", "timestamp": 1647143749000}, "score": 20.481129, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/B9780433305033500316"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[1969]]}, "ISBN": ["9780433305033"], "references-count": 21, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-433-30503-3.50031-6", "published": {"date-parts": [[1969]]}}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 5, 6]], "date-time": "2026-05-06T11:13:40Z", "timestamp": 1778066020154, "version": "3.51.4"}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Elsevier BV", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["SSRN Journal"], "abstract": "<jats:p>The convergence of decentralised computing paradigms, autonomous artificial intelligence (AI) agents, and distributed ledger technologies is reshaping the cybersecurity landscape in profound and previously unanticipated ways. This systematic literature review synthesises 140 peer-reviewed studies published between 2017 and 2026 to provide a comprehensive examination of security, privacy, and trust in agentic and decentralised AI systems. Following PRISMA 2020 guidelines, the review spans eight thematic pillars: foundations of decentralised and agentic AI architectures; threat models in distributed and autonomous settings; privacy-preserving learning mechanisms; cryptographic foundations; blockchain and distributed ledger integration; IoT and edge AI security; Byzantine resilience and trust; and open research challenges. The findings reveal that whilst federated learning (FL) substantially reduces raw-data exposure, gradient-level attacks, model poisoning, Byzantine failures, and the privacy-utility trade-off remain critical unsolved problems. Blockchainbased governance shows promise for auditability and incentive alignment, yet faces scalability and latency constraints in real-time agentic deployments. The review identifies a pressing need for standardised benchmarks, formal threat models for long-horizon autonomous agents, and deeper integration of post-quantum cryptographic primitives.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.2139/ssrn.6634778", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 5, 6]], "date-time": "2026-05-06T10:32:59Z", "timestamp": 1778063579000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Security, Privacy, and Trust in Agentic AI: A Systematic Literature Review of Decentralised and Agentic AI Systems"], "prefix": "10.2139", "author": [{"given": "Saeed", "family": "Ahmadi", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "78", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "container-title": ["SSRN Electronic Journal"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 5, 6]], "date-time": "2026-05-06T10:32:59Z", "timestamp": 1778063579000}, "score": 20.235035, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.ssrn.com/abstract=6634778"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.6634778", "ISSN": ["1556-5068"], "issn-type": [{"value": "1556-5068", "type": "electronic"}], "published": {"date-parts": [[2026]]}}], "items-per-page": 10, "query": {"start-index": 0, "search-terms": null}}}